<div id="2026-08-25-documentation-book-favicon-public-notice" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-08-25 — Documentation book favicon + production public-doc notice</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Documentation pages (<code>/Documentation/*</code>) now show a book SVG favicon (<code>static/images/favicons/documentation-book.svg</code>) so the tab marks the documentation branch at a glance. A banner also appears when a <strong>public</strong> doc (<code>roles</code> empty or <code>guest</code> in META) is served on a <strong>production</strong> host, reading "You are reading public documentation on a production deployment."</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>How.</strong> <code>Documentation.pm</code> stashes <code>documentation_favicon</code> and <code>doc_is_public</code> on every doc view (registered + unregistered paths). <code>Header.tt</code> prefers <code>documentation_favicon</code> over the site favicon. <code>layout.tt</code> renders the notice when <code>doc_is_public</code> is set and <code>system_identifier</code> matches <code>(?i)production</code>. Banner is themed via <code>var(--*)</code> in <code>base.css</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Signal "this is the documentation branch" in the UI, and make it explicit to readers when they are viewing public reference docs on a live production deployment.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>static/images/favicons/documentation-book.svg</code>, <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Documentation.pm</code>, <code>Comserv/root/Header.tt</code>, <code>Comserv/root/layout.tt</code>, <code>Comserv/root/static/css/base.css</code>.</p>
</div>
